\par\par \b \uc2  Israeli shekel gains against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 198 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 13 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel gained ground against the dollar but weakened against the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the mark and the yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the basket's gains to market speculation that the Bank of Israel would change the relative weights of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  comprising the basket. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman denied this. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in trade today and has in fact not given any announcement pertaining to any intention to change the basket in any way," a dealer at United Bank Mizrahi said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar was weaker in Israel after losing ground around the world. \par \par \uc2  The shekel closed the daily tender at 3.0170 shekels per dollar against Friday's rate of 3.0240. The basket closed at 3.3862 shekels per basket unit against 3.3855 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 3.0583 shekels per 100 yen against 3.0549 on Friday and against the mark at 1.9864 shekels per mark from 1.9784 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.0140 shekels. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr2d013hf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
