\par\par \b \uc2  Shekel weakens against major foreign  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 231 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Feb 8 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel weakened against major foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third consecutive day as local operators followed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lead by purchasing dollars. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning by buying dollars," said Guy Levy of Bank Leumi. He said local operators started buying up large numbers of dollars as well. \par \par \uc2  The shekel closed the daily tender at 3.0290 shekels per dollar, against Tuesday's rate of 3.0220 shekels per dollar. The basket unit closed at 3.3861 shekels per basket unit, against 3.3814 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 3.0524 shekels per 100 yen, against 3.0445 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 1.9750 shekels per DM, from 1.9739 shekels per DM Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In mid-afternoon the shekel traded at 3.0267 shekels per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "People feel that domestic interest rates on the shekel will drop soon," Levy said. "The dollar in the world was static today, so the strengthening of the shekel and the basket unit against the dollar is the result of local activity." \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 3.0524 per 100 yen, against 3.0445 on Tuesday, and against the mark at 1.9750 shekels from 1.9739 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011103dr2800ist\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
