\par\par \b \uc2  Shekel strengthens, Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 1995\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1995 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TEL AVIV, Jan 5 (Reuter) - The Israeli shekel strengthened against the dollar, which weakened around the world, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Israel intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times to prop up the basket of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The shekel closed the daily tender at 3.0240 shekels per dollar against Wednesday's rate of 3.0280. The basket closed at 3.3641 shekels per basket unit aginst 3.3651 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Trade was characterised by a large supply of dollars and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and volume was high. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors were attracted to high interest rates on shekel holdings. \par \par \uc2  "The trend will probably continue until the shekel is devalued," a dealer at First International Bank said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it will not devalue the shekel. \par \par \uc2  On the crosses the shekel traded against the yen at 2.9901 shekels per 100 yen against 2.9911 on Wednesday and against the mark at 1.9427 shekels per mark from 1.9402 on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon the dollar was trading at 3.0280 shekels. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1995 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011104dr1501e3z\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\